":null,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":0.03953040187886914,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":55.8,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.0990782440747926,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":74.5,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.051304556762672794,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":68.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.03402243974891972,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":7.5,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.021132343032294148,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":64.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.01052,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":7.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Broadstone Net Lease, Inc. is an industrial-focused, diversified net lease REIT that invests in primarily single-tenant commercial real estate properties that are net leased on a long-term basis to a diversified group of tenants. Utilizing an investment strategy underpinned by strong fundamental credit analysis and prudent real estate underwriting, as of September 30, 2026, BNL's diversified portfolio consisted of 767 individual commercial properties with 760 properties located in 44 U.S. states and seven properties located in four Canadian provinces across the industrial, retail, and other property types. Broadstone Net Lease, Inc. was established and incorporated on October 18th, 2017, in Maryland","ceo_bio":"Mr. John D. Moragne J.D. | CEO & Director | Age 42 | Compensation: $2.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 62 people. Revenue per employee of $7.3M ranks in the top quartile among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 12%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $4.4M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $155K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Broadstone Net Lease, Inc. is a mid-cap real estate business with a $3.5B market cap on $454M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $270M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 59 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.10\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 15.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 5.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.9) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Real Estate peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Real Estate peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 35% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Reviewing W.P. Carey (NYSE:WPC) & Broadstone Net Lease (NYSE:BNL)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/reviewing-w-p-carey-nysewpc-broadstone-net-lease-nysebnl.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794597309.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.924,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Price-Driven Insight from (BNL) for Rule-Based Strategy","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/43/Price-Driven_Insight_from_BNL_for_Rule-Based_Strategy_111026053802_1794307082.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794307082.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Broadstone Net Lease (BNL) Could Be 20% Undervalued On Earnings And Dividend Lift","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nyse-bnl/broadstone